        "original_id": "783a1be9-eb65-527a-9953-2ddee94206d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Avakian, Bobby Managoff, Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis\n- Companies: Columbia Records, National Wrestling Alliance\n- Works: Jazz on a Summer's Day\n- Roles: record producer, executive, musical director, professional wrestler\n\nFacts:\n- George Avakian was born on March 15, 1919.\n- Bobby Managoff, born Robert Manoogian Jr., was born on January 4, 1918 and died on April 3, 2002.\n- George Avakian was an American record producer and executive known for his work with Columbia Records.\n- George Avakian produced albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis, and other notable jazz musicians.\n- George Avakian was the musical director of the film Jazz on a Summer's Day.\n- Bobby Managoff was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent best known for his work with the National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "74d25bf8-6ee5-56f1-bc34-8e262588078d",
        "text": "Page: George Avakian. Sentence: George Avakian (Armenian: Գևորգ Ավագյան ; Russian: Геворк Авакян ; born March 15, 1919) is an American record producer and executive known particularly for his work with Columbia Records, and his production of albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis and other notable jazz musicians.\nPage: Bobby Managoff. Sentence: Robert Manoogian Jr. (January 4, 1918 – April 3, 2002) was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent who was best known for his work with National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s as Bobby Managoff.\nPage: Jazz on a Summer's Day. Sentence: The Columbia Records jazz producer, George Avakian, was the musical director of the film.",
